--- a/ops/vps/ru/README.md
+++ b/ops/vps/ru/README.md
@@ -798,3 +798,87 @@
 are kept; older ones are in the off-host sets), with the lobby and the Account API
 stopped: `runuser -u postgres -- pg_restore --clean --if-exists -d omoba_ru < <dump>`.
 Never drop the database or delete match directories.
+
+## C4: continuous WAL and physical recovery (review candidate)
+
+This kit requires pgBackRest2.58 or newer in addition to the signed nightly logical
+archive. Bootstrap installs the distribution package, the helper, a protected
+placeholder profile and a minute archive-check timer. It does not add package
+repositories, generate credentials, initialize remote storage, change PostgreSQL
+settings or restart a cluster. An old package or an unconfigured profile fails
+readiness. Review the available package/version before applying bootstrap.
+
+The physical repository uses pgBackRest AES-256-CBC and native checksums. Existing
+GnuPG signatures continue to protect the independent logical archives. Full
+physical copies are taken weekly (or on first run), differentials daily; keep
+three completed full copies and14 differentials. Native expiry retains the WAL
+needed by retained copies. The default provides roughly14–21 days of physical
+recovery after three weekly fulls exist; actual storage/RPO/RTO require a drill.
+A failed PITR phase reports failure while the independent signed logical copy
+still uploads. Its separate success record is not a combined success certificate.
+
+### Operator setup, after the separate host approval
+
+1. Verify PostgreSQL's actual major/data directory/socket and pgBackRest version.
+   The helper checks the live cluster identity/data path before physical work.
+2. Fill `/etc/pgbackrest/omoba-ru.conf` from the placeholder profile. Use an
+   independently operated RU SFTP or S3 repository with its own `/omoba-ru/pitr`
+   prefix. The operator verifies the storage location and failure domain.
+3. Keep the config root:postgres0640 in a root-owned0755 directory. Put the
+   physical repository's SSH private key directly in that directory with
+   root:postgres0640 (or postgres0600), its public key and provider-verified pinned
+   known_hosts beside it. All these files must be direct children and included in
+   secrets escrow. The logical archive uses its existing separate root0600 key.
+   `/etc/pgbackrest/empty` must be protected and empty; ambient pgBackRest options
+   are discarded. No credential is accepted on the command line.
+4. Run `ru_backup.py pitr-config --json` for the protected-profile check and exact
+   public archive command. Initialize the stanza with pgBackRest, explicitly
+   naming the same config, empty include directory and `omoba-ru` stanza as that
+   output. Use a clean environment and run the native command as postgres.
+5. Separately review/apply PostgreSQL `archive_mode=on`, `archive_timeout=60s`,
+   empty `archive_library`, and the exact emitted `archive_command`. Schedule any
+   required cluster restart through the normal drain/owner process. The helper
+   refuses a different command, async archive mode or a dropping queue limit.
+6. Escrow the protected config, cipher passphrase, keys and backup.env with the
+   established encrypted secrets procedure. A lost cipher passphrase makes the
+   physical archive unreadable. No real secret is supplied by the repository.
+7. Run the normal `ru_backup.py backup --reason manual`, `drill`,
+   `pitr-check --alert` and `check --json --remote`. The combined drill verifies the
+   signed logical snapshot plus a fresh named physical recovery target. RU
+   readiness requires an initial successful physical drill, not a grace period.
+
+S3 alternative: replace the SFTP-specific options with `repo1-type=s3`, the
+provider's `repo1-s3-endpoint`, `repo1-s3-bucket`, `repo1-s3-region`, access key and
+secret in this same protected file, `repo1-storage-verify-tls=y`, and the separate
+repository prefix. Never disable TLS verification. The checked local integration
+uses SFTP; the actual selected provider still requires the independent-storage
+and RU restore drill before deployment acceptance.
+
+### Health and restore boundaries
+
+`omoba-pitr-check-ru.timer` proves an actual WAL archive round every minute. Failed
+checks alert using the established journal/Telegram path. A dedicated locked
+PITR notification journal cannot overwrite long-running backup metadata. Normal
+backup health rejects a failed or older-than5-minute archive proof, physical base
+older than26h, missing/failed/older-than35-day physical drill, weak settings or
+missing escrow. `check --remote` also reads the actual physical repository without
+refreshing local success. The host refuses disabled PITR for a production launch.
+
+The scratch cluster lives in `/var/lib/omoba-ru-pitr`, independently traversable
+by postgres. The helper reserves space, creates a fresh owned directory/socket,
+restores only there, strips source network/preload/streaming settings, exposes no
+TCP listener and disables archiving on the restored cluster. It requires a
+completed named-target promotion, source system identifier, schema histories and
+WAL replay position. Merely accepting read-only connections is not success.
+Cleanup is mandatory; an un-stoppable scratch cluster is retained and reported as
+failure. No restore uses `--delta` or overwrites a primary directory.
+
+For a real incident, restore secrets and the selected pgBackRest archive to a new
+host of the same PostgreSQL major. Select the operator-approved point/time and a
+new empty data directory with the native pgBackRest restore command. Start it
+with reviewed isolated settings, prove recovery/data first, then switch services
+through a separate approved deployment. The automated drill never performs that
+switch or a production restore.
+
+The local proof uses real career10/portal11 data structures and explicit synthetic
+receipts in separate local containers; it is not an independent-host/RU RPO proof.
